            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Russian for a prince, then the Russian for a kingdom."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: рыцарь",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "рыцарь (rýtsar) — \"a knight\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Рыцарь сел на коня и уехал. Rýtsar sel na konyá i uyékhal. The knight got on his horse and rode off."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Genitive рыцаря."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "рыцарь (rýtsar) was borrowed through Polish rycerz from German Ritter \"a rider, a knight\" (EtymDB)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
